    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="1587ba1a-f44f-51b9-9715-b45978c3b836" activityNameId="7e287bb4-c6df-54f3-8abd-42d390f31c25" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production IR, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production IR, at long-distance pipeline
In 2023 100% of the imported Iraqi natural gas to IQ was imported by pipeline and 0% as LNG. An average distance of 1000 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Iran, of which are 0 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are 0 km. The net calorific value of natural is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=6ab4706a-0135-3be6-a6f5-3c5649961835
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Iraqi natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location: The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2023.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6ab4706a-0135-3be6-a6f5-3c5649961835.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
